@meta
id: 17-02
title: Ctrl-O walks back through your jumps
chapter: 17
type: lesson
skills: jump-back, jumplist
par: 140
minutes: 6
vscode: Alt+Left, Alt+Left
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
A review left three comments on this provider. Start by searching for
`order_confirmation`, which is the first of them: the template should be
called `order_created`. Leave it for now, because the other two are
further away and you want to deal with them while you remember.

Second comment, at the bottom: `refundPartial` should also mark the
order as refunded. Its update values need `status: 'REFUNDED'` after
`refundedAmount: amount`.

Third comment, back up in `ship`: the error code `ORDER_NOT_PENDING`
should be `ORDER_NOT_SHIPPABLE`.

Then return to the first comment and fix the template. You made two
jumps to get away from it, so two apostrophes will not get you back:
they only remember one step. There is a key that remembers all of them.

All three edits are graded.

@keys
| `Ctrl-O` | back one jump; press again for the jump before that |
| `''` | back one jump, and only one |
| `t}` | up to just before the closing brace |
| `ciw` | change the word under the cursor |

@hints
`''` after two jumps takes you to the wrong place: the `ship` line you
just left is where the second jump started. You need the position two
jumps ago.
--
`Ctrl-O` goes back one entry in the jumplist and can be pressed
repeatedly. Two presses here.
--
`/order_confirmation`, then `/refundedAmount` and `t}` to insert
`, status: 'REFUNDED'`, then `?ORDER_NOT_PENDING` and `ciw`. Now
`Ctrl-O` `Ctrl-O` lands you on `order_confirmation`, and `ciw` again.

@solution
    /order_confirmation<Enter>
    /refundedAmount<Enter> t}i, status: 'REFUNDED'<Esc>
    ?ORDER_NOT_PENDING<Enter> ciwORDER_NOT_SHIPPABLE<Esc>
    Ctrl-O Ctrl-O ciworder_created<Esc> :wq<Enter>

`Ctrl-O` is Alt+Left with a memory. Every jump pushes a position onto
the jumplist, and `Ctrl-O` pops them one at a time, in reverse, for as
long as you keep pressing it. Three jumps out, three presses home.

It is also exact. `''` puts you at the start of the line; `Ctrl-O` puts
you on the character you left, which is why `ciw` worked straight away
without a `w` or an `f` to find the word again.

Watch what the second `Ctrl-O` did *not* do. You edited the
`refundedAmount` line after jumping to it, and the edit moved the
cursor. `Ctrl-O` did not care: the jumplist stores where you were when
you jumped *away*, so the landing spot is the one you left, wherever
the cursor had wandered to in between.

Press `Ctrl-O` one more time than you need and you will end up at the
top of the file, because opening it counted as the first jump. Or, since
vim saves the jumplist between sessions, in whatever file you were
editing yesterday. The next lesson shows you the list itself so you can
stop guessing.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_confirmation' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_PENDING');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async refundPartial(id: string, amount: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (amount > order.total) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id, amount);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { refundedAmount: amount },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { CustomerProvider } from '../customer/customer.provider';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';
import { EmailService } from '../../infrastructure/services/email.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(CustomerProvider) protected customerProvider: CustomerProvider,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
    @inject(EmailService) protected emailService: EmailService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async findByCustomer(customerId: string) {
    await this.customerProvider.findOne(customerId);

    return this.orderRepository.findByCustomer({ customerId });
  }

  public async create(args: { customerId: string; total: number }) {
    const customer = await this.customerProvider.findOne(args.customerId);

    const order = await this.orderRepository.create({
      values: { customerId: customer.id, total: args.total, status: 'PENDING' },
    });

    await this.emailService.send({ orderId: order.id, template: 'order_created' });

    return order;
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status !== 'PENDING') {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_SHIPPABLE');
    }

    await this.orderRepository.update({ where: { id }, values: { status: 'SHIPPED' } });

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async refundPartial(id: string, amount: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (amount > order.total) {
      throw exception('REFUND_EXCEEDS_TOTAL');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id, amount);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { refundedAmount: amount, status: 'REFUNDED' },
    });
  }
}
